[{"result":{"data":{"json":{"id":"368","stub":{"id":"368","section":"04. Indian Meadows Bridge to Lower Narrows Campground","altname":"Lower Rustic","river":"Cache La Poudre","difficulty":"IIItoIV","states":["USA-COL"]},"primaryGaugeStatus":{"status":"below-recommended","latestReading":{"value":"373","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"metric":"cfs","adjustedDifficulty":null},"pointOfInterests":[{"type":"put-in","description":"The low bridge across the Poudre River.","id":"107882","location":{"latitude":"40.700249","longitude":"-105.544227"},"name":"Indian Meadows Low Bridge Put-In","distance":"0.01","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Fishing site and picnic area administered by the Arapaho and Roosevelt National Forests as a day-use area that has river access.","id":"UGRG5Ybm9H3ifMGXpqkj1","location":{"latitude":"40.698873","longitude":"-105.540813"},"name":"Indian Meadows Fishing Site","distance":"0.19","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"rapid","description":"Begins after passing under the Highway 14 Bridge.","id":"6NFjxpSchypwV8E4sMRp1","location":{"latitude":"40.689774","longitude":"-105.509262"},"name":"Grandpa's Gorge","distance":"2.34","difficulty":"III+","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"rapid","description":"A drop directly above the small bridge here where the current pushes to the left and into the concrete foundation of the bridge.","id":"zvi9oErjvKVZp4iJGI6PN","location":{"latitude":"40.674263","longitude":"-105.475946"},"name":"Decapitation Bridge","distance":"5.19","difficulty":"IV","approximate":false,"photoID":null},{"type":"other","description":"Entrance to Mountain Park Campground","id":"HOmNTXkUIDHSQyK2apKKx","location":{"latitude":"40.682669","longitude":"-105.461831"},"name":"Mountain Park Campground","distance":"6.39","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"access","description":"Picnic area with tables and a toilet administered by Arapaho and Roosevelt National Forests located along Highway 14 that provides access to the river.","id":"cmxlud21DQkyT0jSb4KBa","location":{"latitude":"40.690491","longitude":"-105.449884"},"name":"Century Park Picnic Site Access","distance":"7.83","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false},{"type":"takeout","description":"Walk-in tent camgpround administered by Arapaho and Roosevelt National Forests that provides access to the river.","id":"113124","location":{"latitude":"40.688889","longitude":"-105.432575"},"name":"Lower Narrows Campground Take-Out","distance":"9.55","photoID":null,"difficulty":"N/A","approximate":false}],"alerts":[],"photos":[],"detail":{"id":"368","permitUrl":"","permitInfo":"","description":"This is an excellent intermediate run at most levels, with a many class 3 drops and a few places where the drops are III+ or IV at moderate and high levels.  The first noteworty section is Grandpa's Gorge, which the river enters after crossing under the bridge below Indian Meadows.  At moderate to high water, a couple holes in the gorge get sticky - hit them straight and hard or just go around them.  Other highlights are the abrupt drop under the bridge just above the Mountain Park campground, a few outstanding surfing waves at the campground, and the two drops below the brige to the campground.  The first drop below the bridge is a bit messy, but it has a good (if somewhat thin) line through the middle.  A large and tenacious hole forms in the center and right side of the drop at mile marker 99 (which has various dramatic names).  Expecially at high water, hit it hard and keep paddling, or just avoid it to the right.  You can't see this hole from above, so it's been the source of considerable excitement.  At medium flows, there is an exceptional 'beginner play hole' on river right. Also look for the small, but very smooth and eddy-served surfing waves shorty above Century park, where the river merges below an island.\n\nThis run is best above 3.5 on the Pineview gauge, and preferably above 4'.  At 4' and above, it rolls along nicely without getting overly pushy, but also without any real flatwater.\n\nWhile most of this run is near the road, it somehow retains the flavor of a run deeper in the woods.  Both the upper and lower Rustic runs need a bit more water than those below the narrows, so the season will begin later and end earlier.  It's also noticably colder in the upper canyon, and a full day in a play boat up here can be a chilling experience.\n\n**To get there:** The put-in is the Indian Meadows Low Bridge at mile marker 94.  Good take-outs are at the small Century Park picnic area at mile-marker 100, or a bit farther downstream at the Narrows Picnic Area/Campground at mile marker 101.6.  As an alternative, strong beginners can put in below the rapid at mm 99 for a short run. This section from mm 99 to Narrows PA/CG is much more interesting than Filter Plant and less difficult than Bridges.\n\nCheck out [www.allaboutrivers.com](http://www.allaboutrivers.com) [description](http://www.allaboutrivers.com/guides/outputmile.cfm?rivername=Cache%20La%20Poudre%20River&runname=Grandpa%27s%20Gorge) of this reach.\n\nFor descriptions of Colorado runs, see Whitewater of the Southern Rockies by Stafford and McCutchen, or Colorado Rivers and Creeks by Banks and Eckert.\n\nThe most reliable flow information, and a calculator for converting cfs to/from the Pineview gauge, is available from the Poudre Rock Report at [http://www.poudrerockreport.com](http://www.poudrerockreport.com)\n\nLat/longitude coords are approximate, from TopoZone.\n\nSee also,\n\n[Big South](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/365/) (Class V/VI),\n\n[Joe Wright Creek](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2859/) (Class V),\n\n[Spencer Heights](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/369/) (Class V/VI),\n\n[South Fork](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/374/) (Class IV/V),\n\n[White Mile Run/Upper Rustic](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/367/) (Class III),\n\n[Grandpa's Gorge/Lower Rustic](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/368/) (Class III/IV),\n\n[The Narrows](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/370/) (Class IV/V/V+),\n\n[Upper Mishawaka](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/371/) (Class III/IV),\n\n[Lower Mishiwaka](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3368/) (Class III),\n\n[Poudre Park](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3369/) (Class IV),\n\n[Bridges](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/3370/) (Class III/IV),\n\n[Upper North Fork](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/373/) (Class IV/V),\n\n[Lower North Fork](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/2822/) (Class II/III), and\n\n[Filter Plant](http://www.americanwhitewater.org/rivers/id/372/) (Class III).","averageGradient":"43","maxGradient":"0","length":"9.6","correlations":[{"reachID":"368","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":"About 3 to 3.75 ft at Pineview","mediumRunnableRangeComment":"About 3.75 to 4.5 at Pineview","highRunnableRangeComment":"About 4.5 to 5+ at Pineview","aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"650","beginMediumRunnable":"1000","beginHighRunnable":"1800","endHighRunnable":"3000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"CACHE LA POUDRE AT CANYON MOUTH NEAR FORT COLLINS","gaugeSource":"COLORADO_DEPARTMENT_OF_WATER_RESOURCES","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"CLAFTCCO","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"373","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"3.68","dateTime":"2026-05-11T02:45:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"40.66451","longitude":"-105.224188"},"externalSourceLinks":null},"migrationErrorExplanation":null,"comment":null,"status":{"status":"below-recommended","latestR